A||||11||FieroPerformance||Ocelot exhaust? Good or bad?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroPerformance||10-27-2001||12:50 AM||||I need a new muffler, tips, and the pipes that go from the muffler to the tips. I am on a tight budget but I don't want to go cheap. I want a good sound (like stock or louder), none of that bumble bee, coffee can crap. I've heard bad things about the Ocelot exhausts from the FieroStore? Does anyone have it? If so, are you satisfied? What other options are there?<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DR650SE||10-27-2001||12:52 AM||||I have it on an 86 SE and like it.  It sounds good and the tips look good too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroPerformance||10-27-2001||12:54 AM||||Cool. Thanks DR650SE.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||10-27-2001||02:10 AM||||I have it on my car. Sounds nice. Only bad side is the tips are "soft" chromed. So if you do not keep them clean and protected they will pit/rust. You could buy them wothout tips then buy a better set of tips if you want. <P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||10-27-2001||02:55 AM||||I've got one on my GT too and it really didn't make much of a difference in performance. It sounds pretty good though.<BR>As Oreif already said, the tips are "soft"<BR>or as i call them cheap chrome and will rust easily if you drive it in any kind of wet or<BR>salty weather. The pipes, unlike the originals, will rust as well. If you get the Ocelot system I would highly suggest painting the pipes with a high temp paint to help keep the rust down and make them last longer.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000005||Haze_Performance||10-27-2001||04:23 AM||||I have heard the exhaust on Oreif's car. It sounds real good. I'm thinking of getting that one without the tips. (I have aftermarket ones) or a Borla system. (Yet to hear one). A plus in favor of the Borla is, it has all stainless pipes, muffler & tips. It costs quite a bit more but, it should last the life of you car.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">                 .                 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> - Pennocks Wild Rides - <A HREF="http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||12
Z||000006||Rodney||10-27-2001||08:12 AM||||Sometime this winter I hope to be offering my exhaust system. It will be from the crossover back and will include a converter. Polished 304 stainless steel 3" diameter dual tips. The rest of the system will be in two inch 409 stainless steel like OEM. Complete and ready to bolt in. No cutting etc. The flange will be on the pipe to connect to the crossover. The brackets on the front will be welded on for the factory springs. Just bolt in. I'm hoping to sell them at $399.00 and shipping. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||10-27-2001||10:24 AM||||I have heard the Borla system, Gargoyle has one on his car. It sounds nice. Not quite as "raspy" as the Ocelot and a slightly deeper tone. I would have bought the Borla if one was available. You will get better performance gains from the Borla. The Ocelot is a 2" pipe system where the Borla is a 2 1/2" pipe system.<P><BR>Rodney, Would the tips on yours be "adjustable"? The Borla has the tips already welded on and they point straight back. I think the tips look better angled slightly up to follow the contour of the aero effects/ rear fasica.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||10-27-2001||11:25 AM||||Rodney,<P>You *are* da' man!<P>Any chance that these will be available without tips? Or that you could offer an option on different tips? (I want to do square tips, like the early 70's Corvette.)<BR>I understand the upcoming Borla systems will only be available with tips. Merely a suggestion.<P>As for the Ocelot system, a guy in our club has one behind a 3.4. I like the way it sounds. <BR>I describe the sound as a "stock Fiero on steroids". <BR>I'll take "raspy" over "thrum" any day.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Some mornings, it just isn't worth chewing through the restraints.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||10-27-2001||11:41 AM||||I thought the Borla was 2" in diameter. That is what mine measures. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Klown||10-27-2001||06:43 PM||||If Rodney is building an exhaust system, I'm probably gonna buy it for sure.  His products and his service are top notch.  I have his competition short shifter and his getrag rebuild kit.  All I can tell you is that my car shifts better than ever.  I can only imagine that if he sells an exhaust system, it'll be great quality.  When do you expect to be selling it Rodney?||||reg||14
Z||000011||FieroPerformance||10-27-2001||07:42 PM||||I want one. The problem is that I need one soon. My car is going to be road ready in a few weeks and I want the exhaust to be installed before I put the cradle back in.||||reg||1
